  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=x^2-x+5, x>\\frac{1}{2}$, and $\\mathrm{g}(\\mathrm{x})$ is its inverse function, then $\\mathrm{g}^{\\prime}(7)$ equals:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{1}{3}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{13}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{3}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{1}{13}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=y=x^2-x+5$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&x^2-x+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}+5=y \\\\\n&\\left(x-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{19}{4}=y \\\\\n&\\left(x-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2=y-\\frac{19}{4} \\\\\n&x-\\frac{1}{2}=\\pm \\sqrt{y-\\frac{19}{4}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&x=\\frac{1}{2} \\pm \\sqrt{y-\\frac{19}{4}} \\\\\n&\\text { As } x>\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&x=\\frac{1}{2}+\\sqrt{y-\\frac{19}{4}} \\\\\n&g(x)=\\frac{1}{2}+\\sqrt{x-\\frac{19}{4}} \\\\\n&g^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{x-\\frac{19}{4}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\ng^{\\prime}(7)=\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{7-\\frac{19}{4}}}=\\frac{1}{2 \\frac{\\sqrt{28-19}}{2}}=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$"
  }
}